# THE SPEED RATCHET'S CEILINGS: the most each phase of `packages/cli`'s
# own build and check may cost, in milliseconds, ONE MACHINE per row —
# <platform>-<machine>-<cpu> <command> <phase> <ms>. Read by
# `tools/speed_ratchet.py` (`make speed-ratchet`), whose measurement is
# the LEAST of SPEED_ROUNDS warm one-edit rounds (`tools/speed_measure.sh`).
#
# A ceiling MAY ONLY FALL: `--accept` lowers a row to what it measured and
# never raises it. A raise is a human edit of this file, and the diff is the
# review. A machine with no row here is measured and printed, never gated.
#
# A `warm` row is the DB 07 warm-edit gate's (tools/warm_edit_bench.sh,
# judged by speed_ratchet.py --warm): wall ms for `check packages/cli`,
# unchanged and after one body edit, held HARD against the ticket's own
# targets (avra-8sb5.57.176) — unchanged 60 ms, edit 300 ms, goal 150.
# These are targets, not a measured baseline, so they take no ratio;
# `--warm --accept` may only LOWER one to a faster real run, never raise it.
#
# The `ci-warm` rows are the SAME targets for the CI keeper: `keepers-a`
# runs `tools/warm_edit_bench.sh` on the runner with the store prepare
# handed down, and `SPEED_HOST=ci-warm` keys it to the one stable host, so
# a runner's CPU never decides whether the warm gate is judged. A run that
# cannot judge FAILS (a skip is not a pass); only the workflow's
# `warm_skip` input, passed as WARM_EDIT_SKIP, may stand it down.
#
# A `wall` row is the PR check's own clock (tools/ci_wall.py, judged by
# speed_ratchet.py --wall in the `test` job): `ci-wall wall <job> <ms>` and
# `ci-wall wall total <ms>`, held HARD. `total` is the sum of the jobs'
# own clocks, so no queue between them inflates it.
#
# The `ci-wall` ceilings are the FULL-GATE PR's: the merge queue is gone and
# the PR itself is the gate (keepers, seed-check and the suites included), so
# a PR that builds its own compiler costs ~16 min of `prepare` and ~70 min of
# summed job clock. They were first set for the fast floor and refused every
# PR; these are calibrated from the completed runs that measured the gate.
ci-wall wall gate 650000
ci-wall wall prepare 1300000
ci-wall wall total 7000000
ci-warm warm edit 300
ci-warm warm unchanged 60
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc build analyze 1742
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc build emit 983
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc build keep 6704
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc build link 1829
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc build lower 2491
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc check analyze 1768
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc check keep 6835
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc check lower 2568
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc warm edit 300
linux-x86-64-amd-epyc warm unchanged 60
